property_value: NCIT:P325 "A class of pharmaceutical agents made from living organisms or their products that includes recombinant proteins, antibodies, and nucleic acids." xsd:string {NCIT:P378="NICHD"}
property_value: NCIT:P325 "A product of biological origin applicable to the prevention, treatment, or cure of a disease or condition, for example: virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, vaccine, blood, blood component or derivative, allergenic product, or analogous product." xsd:string {NCIT:P378="ICH"}
property_value: NCIT:P325 "A product of biological origin applicable to the prevention, treatment, or cure of a disease or condition, for example: virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, vaccine, blood, blood component or derivative, allergenic product, or analogous product. (FDA 21 CFR 600.3)" xsd:string {NCIT:P378="CDISC"}
property_value: NCIT:P325 "A product of biological origin applicable to the prevention, treatment, or cure of a disease or condition. Such products may include virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, vaccine, blood, blood component or derivative, allergenic product, protein, or analogous product. NOTE: Biological products may be produced through biotechnology in a living system, such as a microorganism, plant cell, or animal cell. Biological products are generally large, complex molecules and are often more difficult to characterize than small molecule drugs. [After 21 CFR 600.3; After FDA Biological Product Definitions] See also vaccine, cell therapy, gene therapy, pharmaceutical product, drug product, medicinal product." xsd:string {NCIT:P378="CDISC-GLOSS"}
property_value: NCIT:P325 "A substance made from a living organism or thing it produces.  EXAMPLE(S): virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, vaccine, blood, blood component or derivative, allergenic product, analogous product  OTHER NAME(S):  NOTE(S):" xsd:string {NCIT:P378="BRIDG 5.3"}
property_value: NCIT:P325 "A substance made from living organisms or things they produce. EXAMPLE(S): virus, therapeutic serum, toxin, antitoxin, vaccine, blood, blood component or derivative, allergenic product, analogous product" xsd:string {NCIT:P378="BRIDG 3.0.3"}
property_value: NCIT:P325 "A substance that is made from a living organism or its products and is used in the prevention, diagnosis, or treatment of cancer and other diseases. Biological agents include antibodies, interleukins, and vaccines." xsd:string {NCIT:P378="NCI-GLOSS"}
property_value: NCIT:P366 "Biological_Agent" xsd:string

