[Term]
id: NCIT:C1005
name: Arsenic Trioxide
def: "A small-molecule arsenic compound with antineoplastic activity.  The mechanism of action of arsenic trioxide is not completely understood. This agent causes damage to or degradation of the promyelocytic leukemia protein/retinoic acid receptor-alpha (PML/RARa) fusion protein; induces apoptosis in acute promyelocytic leukemia (APL) cells and in many other tumor cell types; promotes cell differentiation and suppresses cell proliferation in many different tumor cell types; and is pro-angiogenic. (NCI04)" [] {NCIT:P378="NCI"}
